# Engineering context and tool routing

This checklist applies to every Plan-mode and Agent-mode prompt. A pure comprehension question that does not involve code, architecture, or a plan may be answered without these runs.

Before `CreatePlan` or any file edit:

1. Query GBrain about the task (`user-gbrain`). It holds prior decisions that are not in the code. If the result is empty, say so and continue from the source tree.
2. Graphify for structure and impact. If `graphify` is not on PATH, use `%USERPROFILE%\.local\bin\graphify.exe`. If `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing, run `graphify extract . --code-only --no-cluster` first. Run `graphify query` before a broad structural search.
3. Read and follow the matching Superpowers skill. `writing-plans` before a plan. `test-driven-development` before implementation. `systematic-debugging` for a bug. `verification-before-completion` before claiming the work is done. Do not wrap or replace its bootstrap.
4. Use Context7 (`user-Context7`) when the task depends on a library, SDK, API, or CLI, before answering from memory.
5. Before the first edit of the affected files, read the matching engineering standard. The short summary below does not replace that file.
6. After a change, review, audit, or fix, read and follow the matching gstack skill (`/gstack-review`, `/gstack-qa`, `/gstack-investigate`), unless the active engineering-fix skill forbids that extra review.

| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| **GBrain** | Durable project knowledge, history, previous decisions |
| **Graphify** | Structural codebase understanding and change-impact analysis |
| **Superpowers** | Engineering method: planning, TDD, debugging, verification |
| **gstack** | Review and QA after a change, review, audit, or fix |
| **Context7** | Current library, SDK, API, and CLI documentation |

## Rust

When creating, modifying, reviewing, or refactoring Rust, follow `rust-engineering-standard.mdc` (plugin rule; attaches on `*.rs` / Cargo files). Correctness, memory/concurrency safety, and explicit invariants come before cleverness or hypothetical performance. Do not use `unwrap()`/`expect()` for expected runtime failure.

HTTP/API with Axum, Tokio, and Tower additionally follows `rust-axum-engineering-standard.mdc`. Handlers are transport adapters: extract, invoke one application operation, map the result. Domain types must not return HTTP status codes.

Persistence with SQLx and PostgreSQL follows `rust-sqlx-engineering-standard.mdc`. SQL is architecture, not an implementation detail. Domain types must not depend on `PgPool` / `Transaction`.

Testing and quality follow `testing-quality-engineering-standard.mdc`. Test behavior and invariants, not coverage percentage. Use the lowest layer that reliably proves the behavior.

Security and supply chain follow `security-supply-chain-engineering-standard.mdc`. Least privilege, fail closed; secrets must not be logged or committed.

Rig/agentic systems additionally follow `rust-rig-agentic-engineering-standard.mdc`. Rig is orchestration, not architecture. Domain types must not depend on `rig::Agent`.

Logging, tracing, and observability follow `observability-logging-tracing-engineering-standard.mdc`. Spans, structured fields, and filters are the mechanism; domain standards keep their own policy.

## Engineering audits

Repository-wide or scoped engineering audits use plugin skills under `skills/engineering/`.

- Rust: `/rust-engineering-audit` and `/rust-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/rust/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. The process skill reads `references/rust-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/rust-engineering-standard.mdc` (same body; the `.mdc` keeps Cursor globs).
- Axum/HTTP: `/rust-axum-engineering-audit` and `/rust-axum-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/axum/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. Both skills read `skills/engineering/_standards/rust-axum-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/rust-axum-engineering-standard.mdc`.
- Testing: `/testing-quality-engineering-audit` and `/testing-quality-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/testing/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. Both skills read `skills/engineering/_standards/testing-quality-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/testing-quality-engineering-standard.mdc`.
- Security: `/security-supply-chain-engineering-audit` and `/security-supply-chain-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/security/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. Both skills read `skills/engineering/_standards/security-supply-chain-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/security-supply-chain-engineering-standard.mdc`. Never reproduce secrets.
- Rig/agentic: `/rust-rig-agentic-engineering-audit` and `/rust-rig-agentic-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/rig/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. Both skills read `skills/engineering/_standards/rust-rig-agentic-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/rust-rig-agentic-engineering-standard.mdc`.
- SQLx/PostgreSQL: `/rust-sqlx-engineering-audit` and `/rust-sqlx-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/sqlx/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. Both skills read `skills/engineering/_standards/rust-sqlx-postgresql-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/rust-sqlx-engineering-standard.mdc`.
- Observability, logging, and tracing: `/observability-logging-tracing-engineering-audit` and `/observability-logging-tracing-engineering-fix`. Fix is allowed only against a completed open audit in `docs/engineering-audits/observability/`; never invent findings or silently re-audit in fix mode. Both skills read `skills/engineering/_standards/observability-logging-tracing-engineering-standard.md`, which must stay in sync with `rules/observability-logging-tracing-engineering-standard.mdc`.

Project-specific rules in `AGENTS.md` take precedence over this global routing.
